<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil steady, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil steady, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were almost steady on Thursday in central Indian markets, traders said.</p>
<p>The underetone was steady as the markets welcomed October rains, which traders said would help the standing soybean crop.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm on limited selling. Soyoil solvent was up by 1,200 rupees and soyoil refined by 1,000 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were down on reduced export demand. Soymeal yellow was $275 per tonne for November, December and January shipment in the 1996/97 (November/October). Rapeseed extraction was quoted at $118 per tonne for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was offered at 4,000 rupees (f.o.r) Bedibunder and at 3,950-3,975 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
